<title>UK: Bank of Scotland sets 150 mln stg perpetual bond. [CORRECTED 09:52 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bank of Scotland sets 150 mln stg perpetual bond. [CORRECTED 09:52 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers BZW and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF SCOTLAND</p>
<p> AMT    150 MLN STG   COUPON     8.375 PCT MATURITY    PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.11     PAY DATE    30.OCT.96</p>
<p> SPREAD     +92 BP    MOODY	A1	  LISTING     LONDON</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A-	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> (Corrects S&amp;P rating)</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA (2)</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   FULL FEES  0.625 PCT</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.50 PCT 2006 GILT  NOTES	CALLABLE ON 30.OCT.06 (Corrects from 30.NOV.06) 		AND EVERY FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>		THEREAFTER, IF NOT CALLED COUPON RESET AT +192 BP</p>
<p>		OVER THE THEN-FIVE-YEAR GILT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
